// ANTI-PATTERN: doing role checks inside the login/identity step
public boolean login(String user, String pass) {
    User u = repo.findByUsername(user);
    if (!encoder.matches(pass, u.getPassword())) return false;
    if (!u.getRole().equals("ADMIN")) return false; // WRONG: authZ in authN
    return true; // non-admins can't even log in -> bug, not security
}
```
*Permission checks don't belong in the identity step — keep the two concerns separate.*

